id: bog-environment
name: Bog Environment
kind: battlefield
environment: true
hardnessMin: 0
hardnessMax: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Mud to the knees. Every Combat Roll 1(bT) worse and your Speed halved for as long as
  you are in it. Hardness Rank 0 or 1, the ARC's to pick.
text: >
  Bog Environment: A harsh environment where the ground is a bog, sapping the strength
  from anyone who finds themselves caught in it.

  Hardness Rank: 0~1 (decided by the ARC)

  Effects: While in this Battle Environment, reduce all of your Combat Rolls by 1(bT)
  and halve your Speed.

---

# The first Environment that does something to a character standing still in it, which
# makes it the first with a script at all.
#
# "While in this Battle Environment" is the whole of the condition, and it is not written
# below: being gathered is what standing in it means. The registry looks up the Environment
# the character is in and compiles that one file, the same way a Combat Condition's script
# does not ask whether the character has it.
#
# --- Every Combat Roll ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce all of your Combat Rolls by 1(bT)."
#
# All of them, which is what `combatRolls` is: it fans out to the Strike, the Dodge and the
# Wound, so one line reaches all three. The same line Vile Weather's top Tier writes, and
# the two stack - a bog in the poison is 2(bT) off everything.
#
# --- The Speed --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Halve your Speed."
#
# Your Speed, singular, so `speed.normal` and not `speed.all`. The distinction is the
# rulebook's own and it is consistent about it: Tornado Weather says "reduce your Speeds",
# plural, and reaches both. Boosted Speed is a named thing of its own, and a bog that
# halved it as well would be a harsher rule than the one written.
#
# `speed.all` is there if this reading is ever corrected - one word, in one place.
#
# A multiplication on the finished value, the way every other halving here is: "when an
# effect multiplies or divides a value, that is applied to the final value".
#
# --- The Hardness Rank -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "0~1 (decided by the ARC)." Mud or the reeds and roots in it. Either way it is the
# softest ground in the game after deep snow, and being thrown into a bog costs almost
# nothing - which is the trade for being slow in it.

[passive]
combatRolls -= 1(bT);
speed.normal *= 0.5;
